An Optimized Model Using LSTM Network for Demand Forecasting  
Abbasimehr, Shabani, and Yousefi (2020) present an optimized Long Short‑Term Memory (LSTM) network for demand forecasting in industrial supply chains. Their approach integrates LSTM with metaheuristic optimization techniques to fine‑tune hyperparameters, improving forecasting accuracy compared to traditional statistical methods and baseline machine learning models. The study demonstrates that LSTM networks capture long‑term dependencies in demand data, reducing forecasting error and enhancing inventory management decisions. This contribution is significant because it validates the role of deep learning in supply chain forecasting, offering a foundation for subsequent work on hybrid and agentic approaches. In the context of Agentic Bullwhip V2, the paper provides a methodological anchor: while LSTM focuses on predictive accuracy, agentic experiments extend the literature toward decentralized coordination and adaptive decision‑making under uncertainty.

